     {
      "text": "80-year-old female presenting with knee pain for 6 years. Character: stiffness with cracking sound; radiation: it does not spread; aggravated by sitting on the floor; relieved by rest. Severity 3/10. Associated: difficulty walking. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 5 years; Hypertension for 7 years; Coronary artery disease, stent 8 years ago. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg; Aspirin 75 mg; Atorvastatin 20 mg. Allergy: peanuts. Family: diabetes. Personal: chews tobacco. Triage: ROUTINE."
